Rule 1 (both tensor operands must have integral dtypes 1–5)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 ∧ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 2 (two tensors must be broadcastable)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 3 (valid out tensor: integral dtype and broadcasted shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≤ 5 ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1) ∧ (if shape(v_1, i) = 1 then shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i) else shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i))
>>
Rule 4 (matching integral dtypes for input, other, and out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (tensor right-shift by integer: nonnegative and within bit-width)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 ∧ v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 1 then v_2 ≤ 7) ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then v_2 ≤ 7) ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 2 then v_2 ≤ 15) ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 3 then v_2 ≤ 31) ∧ (if dtype_(v_1) = 4 then v_2 ≤ 63)
